A||||11||fierospeeder||Discontinued Fiero and Power Steering?||||1||
Z||000000||fierospeeder||12-20-2001||05:04 AM||||Heres a letter from the <BR>Hot Rod December 1988 issue.<P><BR>Straight Steers<P>Since Pontiac has now discontinued the Fiero without ever making a much-needed power steering option available, what would be involved in replacing the manual rack and pinion with a power unit?<BR>               James L Bennett        Atlanta,Georgia<P>For a more responsive, performance-oriented "feel" to the steering, simply remove the stock steering damper.  If you still desire power steering, Zimmer Motor Cars (777 SW 12th Ave., Pompano Beach, FL  33069, 305/943-7600), manufacturers of a custom specialty car based on the Fiero chassis, has power steering conversion pieces applicable to the '87 and earlier v6 Fiero.  Zimmer used a modified Mercury Merkur power steering rack, GM pump 7842630 and pulley 1246472, a special remote reservoir, and custom brackets to hang the assembly on the engine.  All these parts can be purchased from Zimmer.<P>In '88, Pontiac redesigned the entire front suspension.  The projected power steering option was not released for production before the car was canceled, although apparently GM service parts did stockpile some individual components.  As of the summer of '88, the parts computer at Cone Chevrolet (714/525-3508) listed the rack(part No. 26004059), gear outlet hose (26004059), and gear inlet hose (26004058) as "good" numbers.  The special electro-hydraulic power steering pump (7849457) that was to mount up front near the rack has been discontinued, but conceivably, you could use Zimmer's conventional engine-mounted pump with custom hoses.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||12-20-2001||07:41 AM||||Someone please try this, or contact them!!!<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||12-20-2001||07:59 AM||||The Florida Zimmer Co went bankrupt a few years back.  I understand that some on in the Syracuse NY area bought the name and is back making some limited production cars.  None based on the Fiero. <A HREF="http://www.zimmermotorcars.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zimmermotorcars.com</A> <BR> <BR>Zimmer Quicksilver is the Fiero based car.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||WampusCat||12-20-2001||08:02 AM||||Why would ya want power steering in a 2700 pound car?  Just more stuff to break and add unwanted weight.  The manual steering in my car works great.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pyric||12-20-2001||09:17 AM||||I don't know... I'd like to drive one to see what it it was like before passing judgment on if it was worth it.||||reg||1
