Z||000006||Rodney||12-20-2001||10:15 AM||||1988 Mera with 245-50-15 Goodyear Gatorbacks in front. It is a 12.5:1 power steering ratio and was worth it many times over. Makes driving my Mera much more enjoyable. I can make most any turn on the steets with less than 1/2 turn of the steering wheel. One of the best things I did to my Mera. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jefrysuko||12-20-2001||11:50 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kasdan:<BR><B>wait a sec....my power steering car came out of the Pompano/Ft Lauderdale area.....maybe this is a new lead for me?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes Kasdan your system does look very similar to one from Zimmer.<p>[This message has been edited by Jefrysuko (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rodney||12-20-2001||01:59 PM||||When the Zimmer was discontinued Link Racing bought the left over power steering parts. Link Racing then sold the aftermarket power steering kits. I have a Link Racing (Zimmer) power steering kit in my 88 Mera. Old IRM cataloges also show this kit. I bought mine from Link Racing. Link Racing says I am the only one to fabricate steel pressure/return lines to go under the car instead of using the rubber ones they typically supplied. ||||reg||1
