Z||000011||Pyric||12-20-2001||09:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodney:<BR><B>When the Zimmer was discontinued Link Racing bought the left over power steering parts. Link Racing then sold the aftermarket power steering kits. I have a Link Racing (Zimmer) power steering kit in my 88 Mera. Old IRM cataloges also show this kit. I bought mine from Link Racing. Link Racing says I am the only one to fabricate steel pressure/return lines to go under the car instead of using the rubber ones they typically supplied. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'd save up the $$$ for one.  the power steering in my commuter car has me spoiled.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronegS.jpg">     <P><BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
